    "raw": "Given:\n- Nigella's base salary: $3,000\n- Total earnings for the month: $8,000\n- Commission rate: 2%\n- Nigella sells 3 houses\n- House B costs three times as much as House A\n- House C costs twice as much as House A minus $110,000\n\nLet's denote the cost of House A as \\( x \\).\n\nFrom the problem, we can write the following relationships:\n- Cost of House B: \\( 3x \\)\n- Cost of House C: \\( 2x - 110,000 \\)\n\nNigella's total earnings from commissions can be expressed as:\n\\[ 0.02 \\times (x + 3x + (2x - 110,000)) \\]\n\nIncluding her base salary, her total earnings are:\n\\[ 3,000 + 0.02 \\times (x + 3x + (2x - 110,000)) = 8,000 \\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[ 3,000 + 0.02 \\times (6x - 110,000) = 8,000 \\]\n\nSubtract 3,000 from both sides:\n\\[ 0.02 \\times (6x - 110,000) = 5,000 \\]\n\nDivide both sides by 0.02:\n\\[ 6x - 110,000 = 250,000 \\]\n\nAdd 110,000 to both sides:\n\\[ 6x = 360,000 \\]\n\nDivide both sides by 6:\n\\[ x = 60,000 \\]\n\nSo, the cost of House A is $60,000.\n\nFINAL: 60000",
